  "Saved": "Guardado",
  "Give it a name": "Ponle un nombre",
  "A bit bigger, please — draw that one again.": "Un poco más grande, por favor — dibújalo otra vez.",
  "Straight lines are taken as scrolling. Draw a shape with a turn in it.": "Las líneas rectas cuentan como desplazamiento. Dibuja una forma con giro.",
  "Got it. Again.": "Captado. Otra vez.",
  "Looks distinct from the other gestures. Save it.": "Se distingue de los demás gestos. Guárdalo.",
  "Saved, but it can't be used with one finger: it isn't a closed shape": "Guardado, pero no sirve con un dedo: no es una forma cerrada",
  "A cross is two quick diagonal strokes, which is exactly what two flicks look like while scrolling a feed or moving a map. With one finger it would go off by itself.": "Una cruz son dos trazos diagonales iguales al desplazamiento rápido; con un dedo saltaría sola.",
  "This is two straight lines with one corner. Ordinary drags, swipes between photos and the back gesture draw that shape all the time, so with one finger it would go off by itself.": "Son dos líneas con una esquina, muy parecidas al gesto de volver o pasar fotos.",
  "Part of this digit is an open line, and a scroll that curls at the end can look just like it. With one finger it would go off by itself.": "Parte de este dígito es abierta y un desplazamiento curvo se le parece mucho.",
  "A one-finger swipe is how every app scrolls.": "Deslizar un dedo sirve para desplazar en todas las apps.",
  "This digit is an open line that doesn't end where it starts. A curved scroll or swipe in an app can draw the same shape, so with one finger it would go off by itself.": "Este dígito no termina donde empieza, así que un gesto normal podría activarlo.",
  "With one finger only closed shapes are allowed (one stroke that ends where it started), because ordinary scrolls and swipes never do that. This custom gesture isn't drawn that way.": "Con un dedo solo se permiten formas cerradas (un trazo que acaba donde empezó).",
